            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to announce, then the Persian for to state."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تکذیب کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تکذیب کردن (takzib kardan) — \"to refute, to deny (a report)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وزیر این خبر را تکذیب کرد. Vazir in khabar râ takzib kard. The minister denied this report."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For denying a report or a rumour in public. Present takzib mikonad. The opposite is ta'yid kardan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "takzib is usually traced to Arabic takdhīb, \"calling something a lie\"; EtymDB lists no entry. kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
